1. Problem Statement
The Scholarship Office currently manages scholarship requirements using spreadsheets, emails, and paper grade records. This process can result in duplicate semester submissions, unverified academic records, missed deadlines, inconsistent scholarship decisions, and difficulty tracking submission status. The proposed Student Scholarship Monitoring and Academic Compliance System will provide a browser-based platform where scholars can submit academic summaries and evidence, while scholarship staff verify records, evaluate compliance with scholarship policies, and record renewal decisions. The Registrar remains the official source of grades, and the system will not modify official grades or release scholarship payments.
2. Problem, Cause, and Effect
ID	Problem	Cause	Effect
PCE01	Duplicate submissions	Manual spreadsheet recording	Confusing or repeated records
PCE02	Unverified grades	Evidence checked manually	Unreliable evaluation results
PCE03	Missed deadlines	No centralized deadline monitoring	Late submissions and possible deficiencies
PCE04	Inconsistent decisions	Policies applied inconsistently	Unfair or incorrect renewal decisions

3. Scope and Exclusions
In scope:
•	User login and role-based access for scholars and scholarship staff.
•	Scholar registration and scholarship program assignment.
•	Semester academic summary submission and grade-document reference.
•	Duplicate prevention and deadline validation.
•	Verification, return for correction, and resubmission.
•	Compliance evaluation using stored scholarship policy thresholds.
•	Renewal decisions and reasons.
•	Dashboard totals, searching, filtering, and history tracking.
Out of scope:
•	Direct integration with the Registrar's system.
•	Editing official grades or releasing scholarship payments.
•	SMS notifications and machine-learning evaluation.
•	A complete scholarship appeals workflow.
