A3. Requirements and Business Rules (10 points)
1. Functional Requirements
ID	Functional requirement
FR01	The system shall authenticate users and enforce separate Scholar and Scholarship Staff permissions.
FR02	The system shall allow staff to register scholars and assign each scholar to a persisted Merit Scholar or Community Scholar program.
FR03	The system shall allow scholars to submit academic year, semester, GWA, enrolled units, failed subjects, incomplete grades, dropped subjects, and a grade-document reference.
FR04	The system shall record submission timestamps, validate input values, and reject duplicate submissions for the same scholar, academic year, and semester.
FR05	The system shall allow staff to mark submissions Verified or Returned and require a reason when returning a submission.
FR06	The system shall allow scholars to correct and resubmit returned submissions, changing their verification status back to Pending.
FR07	The system shall evaluate only verified submissions using thresholds stored in the scholar's assigned program.
FR08	The system shall display Compliant or With Deficiency and identify every failed policy condition.
FR09	The system shall allow staff to record an Approved or Held renewal decision with notes, preventing approval unless the evaluation is Compliant.
FR10	The system shall display dashboard totals and support searching by scholar name or student ID and filtering by program or compliance result.

2. Non-Functional Requirements
ID	Requirement	Measurement
NFR01	Security	Protected database operations enforce role-based access; unauthorized attempts must be denied in TC08.
NFR02	Performance	Dashboard totals and search results should load within 3 seconds under agreed test conditions.
NFR03	Data integrity	Duplicate submissions and invalid GWA, unit, or count values are rejected by validation and database constraints where applicable.
NFR04	Reliability and auditability	Saved records remain after refresh; verification, evaluation, and renewal changes retain actor, timestamp, and history.

Note: These are proposed measurable targets for the MVP.
3. Business Rules
ID	Business rule
BR01	Merit Scholar requires GWA 1.00–1.75, at least 18 units, zero failed subjects, zero incomplete grades, zero dropped subjects, and a grade-document reference.
BR02	Community Scholar requires GWA 1.00–2.25, at least 15 units, zero failed subjects, zero incomplete grades, no more than one dropped subject, and a grade-document reference.
BR03	A submission cannot be evaluated for final compliance until staff verify its supporting evidence.
BR04	A scholar may have only one submission for each academic year and semester.
BR05	The deadline is October 30, 2026, at 5:00 PM Philippine time. Exactly at the deadline is on time; after it is late.
BR06	Only Scholarship Staff may record renewal decisions. Approval is allowed only when the evaluation is Compliant; a deficient result may be Held but not Approved.

Additional validation: GWA must be 1.00–5.00 inclusive. Enrolled units and failed, incomplete, and dropped counts must be nonnegative integers. Smaller GWA values represent better performance.
Status distinction: Submission status (Pending, Verified, Returned), compliance result (Compliant, With Deficiency), and renewal decision (Approved, Held) are separate. Verified does not automatically mean Compliant or Approved.



