A5. Detailed Use Cases and Data Design (8 points)
1. UC02 — Submit Grades
Field	Description
Use case ID	UC02
Primary actor	Scholar
Trigger	The scholar selects the option to submit semester grades.
Preconditions	The scholar is authenticated, has an assigned program, and is viewing their own account.
Postcondition	A valid submission is saved with timestamp and Pending verification status. Invalid or duplicate submissions are not saved.
Linked requirements	FR01, FR03, FR04, FR06
Linked business rules	BR03, BR04, BR05

Main flow:
7.	The scholar logs in to the system.
8.	The scholar opens the grade submission form.
9.	The system displays the assigned scholarship program.
10.	The scholar selects the academic year and semester.
11.	The scholar enters GWA, enrolled units, failed subjects, incomplete grades, and dropped subjects.
12.	The scholar provides the grade-document reference.
13.	The system validates required fields, allowed values, and uniqueness.
14.	The system records the timestamp and checks the deadline.
15.	The system saves the submission as Pending verification.
16.	The system displays confirmation and submission status.
Alternative and exception flows:
•	A1 — Returned submission: The scholar corrects and resubmits it. Status returns to Pending verification and history is retained.
•	E1 — Invalid input: Invalid GWA or unit/count values trigger an error and are not saved.
•	E2 — Duplicate submission: A duplicate for the same scholar, academic year, and semester is rejected.
•	E3 — Missing evidence reference: The system requires the grade-document reference before accepting the submission.
•	E4 — Late submission: The timestamp is recorded and the late condition is considered during evaluation.
•	E5 — Unauthorized access: A scholar attempting to access another scholar's record is denied.
2. UC07 — Evaluate Compliance
Field	Description
Use case ID	UC07
Primary actor	Scholarship Staff
Trigger	Staff select a verified submission for evaluation.
Preconditions	Staff are authenticated; the submission exists, evidence is Verified, and a program is assigned.
Postcondition	The evaluation result, failed checks, reasons, actor, and timestamp are saved.
Linked requirements	FR01, FR02, FR07, FR08, FR09
Linked business rules	BR01, BR02, BR03, BR05, BR06

Main flow:
17.	Staff log in.
18.	Staff open the dashboard and select a submission.
19.	The system confirms the submission is Verified.
20.	The system retrieves the assigned program and stored policy thresholds.
21.	The system checks GWA, units, failed subjects, incomplete grades, dropped subjects, evidence, and deadline.
22.	The system records each policy check.
23.	If all conditions pass, the result is Compliant.
24.	If any condition fails, the result is With Deficiency and reasons are listed.
25.	The system saves evaluation, staff identity, timestamp, and history.
26.	Staff explicitly record Approved for a Compliant evaluation or Held for a deficient evaluation.
27.	The system saves the decision and notes and displays the updated record.
Alternative and exception flows:
•	A1 — Compliant: Staff may record Approved or Held.
•	A2 — Deficient: The system lists each failed condition; staff may record Held but cannot approve.
•	E1 — Pending verification: Evaluation and approval are blocked until evidence is verified.
•	E2 — Returned submission: The scholar must correct and resubmit before verification and evaluation.
•	E3 — Missing policy assignment: Evaluation is blocked until staff assign a valid program.
•	E4 — Unauthorized action: A scholar attempting to evaluate a record or change a renewal decision is denied.
3. Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD)
 
ERD Design Notes
•	USER_PROFILE stores user identity and role; authentication credentials are handled by Supabase Auth.
•	SCHOLARSHIP_PROGRAM stores thresholds for Merit Scholar and Community Scholar.
•	SCHOLAR_ASSIGNMENT connects a scholar to a scholarship program; SEMESTER_SUBMISSION stores academic summaries and current statuses.
•	VERIFICATION_HISTORY, EVALUATION_HISTORY, and RENEWAL_HISTORY preserve past actions.
•	Enforce uniqueness on (assignment_id, academic_year, semester).
•	Database policies must prevent scholars from reading or changing other scholars' records and from performing staff-only actions.
